"""Per-repository template for tools/build_notebook.py (NOTEBOOK_SPEC 2.2 §4 standalone carrier).

Only the task-specific prose and stage cells live here. Runtime install, the embedded pipeline
modules (pipeline.py, metrics.py, samples.py), and the model pin/stage/verify cells are produced by
the generator from repository sources so they cannot drift from the package.

This template configures an E2E image-text retrieval workflow: the pinned Salesforce/blip-itm-base-coco
snapshot is digest-verified and loaded, the captions of a digest-pinned VizWiz-Captions shard are read
column-only and the 672 photographs of its first two row groups are read the same way, validated and split
by image (row group 0 into train / validation / core test, row group 1 into the test gallery), three drawn
scenes are scored through the inference contract, the frozen model's retrieval over the 391-photograph gallery
is measured beside two non-neural baselines, a bounded fine-tuning of the text encoder's last blocks, both
projections and the ITM head runs, the gallery is scored again per category, the adapted model re-scores the
drawn scenes, and the adapter is exported and reloaded.

Review fixes (Notebook Review Framework v1, review PR #10, ITM-M1..M5 / ITM-m1..m4): the runtime is the fleet's uv
isolated environment (no in-kernel install, no restart); no held-out result is asserted (a kept epoch 0 is reported,
and the export still runs), and the notebook says that the recipe comparisons and the gallery size were decided with
test-gallery numbers, so the test delta is optimistic; every re-run of Sections 5-7 starts from the pretrained model;
the BYOD contract states the enforced minimum, replaces an earlier upload, keeps zip sub-folders under a guarded root
with size limits, names a missing records file, reports the BYOD gallery size and records BYOD provenance; every
measured figure names its run; and the guided layer (how to use, roadmap, predictions, worked answers, a
change-one-thing activity, troubleshooting, glossary, conclusion) is added.
"""
