        "## Glossary\n\n"
        "- **ITC (image-text contrastive) score:** the cosine between an image's and a caption's projected embeddings, "
        "computed separately for each (a dual encoder), so a whole gallery can be ranked cheaply.\n"
        "- **ITM (image-text matching) probability:** a classifier head over a joint encoding of one image with one caption "
        "(a fused encoder); more accurate per pair and far more expensive; not calibrated.\n"
        "- **Gallery:** the set of candidates retrieval ranks — here every caption of every test photograph (image → text) "
        "and every test photograph (text → image).\n"
        "- **Recall@k:** the share of queries whose right answer is among the top k; image → text counts a hit when any of "
        "the photograph's own captions is in the top k.\n"
        "- **Median rank:** the middle position of the right answer over all queries; 1 means at least half are found "
        "first.\n"
        "- **rsum:** the sum of the six recalls (R@1/5/10 in both directions), from 0 to 6.\n"
        "- **Re-ranking:** re-ordering the top candidates of the cheap ITC ranking with the expensive ITM head.\n"
        "- **ITM pair accuracy:** how often the ITM head scores a photograph's own caption above the hardest wrong caption by "
        "ITC.\n"
        "- **Hard negative:** a wrong caption (or photograph) that the model already scores high; training on hard negatives "
        "teaches fine distinctions.\n"
        "- **Baseline:** a system with no model (here chance and a colour-keyword lookup) that shows what any useful model "
        "must beat.\n"
        "- **Fine-tuning / trainable blocks:** further training on labelled examples; only the named text-encoder blocks, the "
        "projections and the ITM head may change, the rest stay frozen.\n"
        "- **Learning rate:** how large each training step is; too large and the model forgets what it knew.\n"
        "- **Epoch / validation selection:** one pass over the training pairs; the epoch kept is the one with the highest "
        "validation rsum (epoch 0 = the frozen model).\n"
        "- **Training / validation / test split:** photographs used to train, to choose the epoch, and to report the final "
        "result once; split by image so no photograph is in two splits.\n"
        "- **Optimistic estimate:** a test score of a configuration whose design was decided by looking at that same test "
        "split.\n"
        "- **Adapter / reload parity:** the saved trained tensors, and the check that a pipeline rebuilt from them gives the "
        "same scores.\n\n"
